1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 { The Italian: the bishop eyes f7, Black's weakest point, and supports a later d4 break. }
3... Bc5
( 3... Nf6 { [%name Two Knights, 4.d3] The Two Knights Defence counter-attacks e4 at once. }
  4. d3 { Calm and solid: White protects e4 and avoids the sharp 4.Ng5 complications. }
  4... Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. Re1 d6 7. c3 { White prepares d4 or a slow Nbd2-f1-g3 regrouping. }
  7... Na5 8. Bb5 a6 9. Ba4 b5 10. Bc2 { The bishop keeps the b1-h7 diagonal and supports a later d4 and kingside play. } )
4. c3 { [%name Giuoco Piano, 5.d4] White prepares d4 to build a broad pawn centre. }
( 4. b4 { [%name Evans Gambit, 5...Ba5] The Evans Gambit: a pawn is offered to gain time for c3 and d4. }
  4... Bxb4
  ( 4... Bb6 { [%name Evans Gambit Declined] Declining is safe; White simply gains queenside space. }
    5. a4 a6 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. Nd5 { The knight jumps into d5, hitting the b6-bishop and the f6-knight. } )
  5. c3 Ba5
  ( 5... Be7 { [%name Evans Gambit, 5...Be7] A solid retreat that keeps the bishop near the king. }
    6. d4 Na5 7. Be2 { The bishop dodges the knight and stays useful; White keeps the big centre. }
    7... exd4 8. Qxd4 { White recaptures with a centralised queen and leads in development for the pawn. } )
  6. d4 { The point of the gambit: c3 and d4 arrive with tempo, opening lines towards Black's king. }
  6... exd4 7. O-O Nge7 8. cxd4 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 { Black returns the pawn to finish development; White has free piece play. } )
4... Nf6
5. d4 { The classical break, striking the centre at once. }
( 5. d3 { [%name Giuoco Pianissimo] The modern main line: quiet build-up with d4 kept in reserve. }
  5... d6 6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 a6 8. Bb3 { The bishop steps away from ...Na5 and ...d5 with tempo. }
  8... Ba7 9. h3 { Stops ...Bg4 and ...Ng4, a standard prophylactic move. }
  9... h6 10. Nbd2 Re8 11. Nf1 { The knight heads for g3, the typical Italian regrouping towards the kingside. } )
5... exd4 6. cxd4 Bb4+ 7. Bd2 Bxd2+ 8. Nbxd2 d5 { Black must strike back in the centre or White's pawns will roll forward. }
9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Qb3 Nce7 11. O-O O-O 12. Rfe1 c6 { White has an isolated d-pawn but active pieces; Black blockades on d5. } *
